            "review_title": "Review at Terrace Al Sham",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nDelicious Find in D7\nFeb 2021\nThis is truly a first class dining experience. The place is a bit basic in appearance but this is soon forgotten as soon as you receive a warm and genuine welcome from the Lebanese owner, and as soon as you see the tempting menu. I ordered falafels, hummus and pitta bread, as well as accidentally ordering baba ganoush. I had mistakenly thought from the picture on the menu that the dish included 2 lots of hummus and had I known it was one serving of hummus and one serving of baba ganoush then I would have ordered something different as I have never been keen on this smoky egg plant dish. However, when it came, to my great surprise, the baba ganoush was absolutely wonderful, full of delightful flavours and I am not sure whether in fact I preferred that or the melt in your mouth hummus. This is the one and only time I have ever enjoyed baba ganoush and I can't wait to go back there and try it again. The pitta bread wasn't quite as good as a freshly baked middle eastern bread would have been but it was very pleasant nonetheless. And the falafels were the best ever tasted, anywhere! They were a real treat for the senses. I lived in Egypt for 5 years so I am used to all sorts of delicious falafels - street food, regular restaurants, fine dining - but I can honestly say that these were the most tasty ever eaten, with an absolutely perfect texture. During the lunch the owner came over to check how I liked the food and it wasn't just a perfunctory gesture. He remained at the table warmly discussing Lebanese food and making friendly small talk and he was a delight to talk to. I didn't eat much else as I had only dropped in for a light lunch but I can't wait to return and try many other things on the menu. My husband has already planned to eat the chicken in breadcrumbs and the Lebanese meat pie which he saw on the on-line menu and I am definitely up for a Lebanese salad, the same falafels, hummus and baba ganoush and any one of the other tempting looking dishes. As the portion size was so generous I ended up taking away half as a takeaway. When I received the box I could see that the owner had added extra baba ganoush to fill up one side of the box so that it looked as full as the other side and had also sliced up a tomato to make an attractive presentation. I don't think that has ever happened to me any other restaurant which has put together a takeaway. Rather it is the norm in many pizza restaurants, for example, to pile pieces of pizza on top of one another in order to squeeze into the smallest box possible, resulting in a sticky mess when unpacking and eating, or many other restaurants often pile all sorts of food food on top of one another, as the easy option. So even the take away box was a delightful surprise in Terrace Al Sham. I can't wait to go again and relive the wonderful culinary experience and I feel very happy that I discovered this fantastic gem.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 25, 2021",
